# Unit02
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 基础词Unit02核心词汇

addition /əˈdɪʃn/ n. 增加；加法 / In addition to English, she also speaks French.
additional /əˈdɪʃənl/ adj. 额外的；附加的 / Additional information can be found on the website.
address /əˈdres/ n./v. 地址；演讲；处理 / The president will address the nation tonight.
adequate /ˈædɪkwət/ adj. 足够的；适当的 / The supply of water is adequate for the community.
adjust /əˈdʒʌst/ v. 调整；适应 / You need to adjust the mirror before driving.
administration /ədˌmɪnɪˈstreɪʃn/ n. 管理；行政 / The administration of the hospital has been improved.
admire /ədˈmaɪər/ v. 钦佩；欣赏 / I admire her courage and determination.
admission /ədˈmɪʃn/ n. 承认；入场 / Admission to the concert is free for children.
admit /ədˈmɪt/ v. 承认；准许进入 / He admitted that he had made a mistake.
adolescent /ˌædəˈlesnt/ n./adj. 青少年 / Adolescents often face peer pressure at school.
adopt /əˈdɑːpt/ v. 采用；收养 / They decided to adopt a child from overseas.
adult /əˈdʌlt/ n./adj. 成年人 / Adults should set a good example for children.
advance /ədˈvæns/ v./n. 前进；进步 / Technology continues to advance at a rapid pace.
advanced /ədˈvænst/ adj. 先进的；高级的 / She is taking an advanced course in mathematics.
advantage /ədˈvæntɪdʒ/ n. 优势；好处 / Being bilingual is a great advantage in today's job market.
adventure /ədˈventʃər/ n. 冒险；奇遇 / Traveling abroad is always an adventure.
advertise /ˈædvərtaɪz/ v. 做广告；宣传 / The company plans to advertise its new product on TV.
advice /ədˈvaɪs/ n. 建议；忠告 / She gave me some useful advice on how to study.
advise /ədˈvaɪz/ v. 建议；通知 / The doctor advised him to quit smoking.
advocate /ˈædvəkeɪt/ v./n. 提倡；倡导者 / She advocates for equal rights for all citizens.
affair /əˈfeər/ n. 事务；事件 / The government is dealing with foreign affairs.
affect /əˈfekt/ v. 影响；感动 / The drought seriously affected crop production.
afford /əˈfɔːrd/ v. 负担得起；提供 / Many families cannot afford to buy a house.
afraid /əˈfreɪd/ adj. 害怕的；恐惧的 / She is afraid of speaking in public.
after /ˈæftər/ prep./conj. 在…之后 / After the rain, the air became fresh.
afternoon /ˌæftərˈnuːn/ n. 下午 / We have a meeting scheduled for this afternoon.
again /əˈɡen/ adv. 再次；又 / Please say that again more slowly.
against /əˈɡenst/ prep. 反对；对着 / The vote was 60 against 40 in favor.
age /eɪdʒ/ n. 年龄；时代 / Children of all age groups are welcome.
agency /ˈeɪdʒənsi/ n. 代理机构 / The travel agency offers package tours to Europe.
agenda /əˈdʒendə/ n. 议程；日程 / The main agenda for today's meeting is the budget.
agent /ˈeɪdʒənt/ n. 代理人；特工 / He works as a real estate agent.
aggressive /əˈɡresɪv/ adj. 侵略性的；有进取心的 / The company adopted an aggressive marketing strategy.
ago /əˈɡoʊ/ adv. 以前 / The incident happened two years ago.
agree /əˈɡriː/ v. 同意；一致 / I agree with your proposal completely.
agreement /əˈɡriːmənt/ n. 协议；一致 / Both parties signed the agreement yesterday.
agriculture /ˈæɡrɪkʌltʃər/ n. 农业 / Agriculture is the backbone of the country's economy.
ahead /əˈhed/ adv. 在前面；提前 / Please look ahead while driving.
aid /eɪd/ n./v. 帮助；援助 / The government sent aid to the disaster area.
aim /eɪm/ v./n. 瞄准；目标 / The aim of the project is to reduce pollution.
air /eər/ n. 空气；气氛 / The air quality has improved significantly.
aircraft /ˈeərkræft/ n. 飞机；航空器 / The aircraft landed safely despite the storm.
airline /ˈeərlaɪn/ n. 航空公司 / The airline offers flights to over 100 destinations.
airport /ˈeərpɔːrt/ n. 机场 / We arrived at the airport two hours early.
alarm /əˈlɑːrm/ n./v. 警报；使惊恐 / The fire alarm went off in the middle of the night.
album /ˈælbəm/ n. 相册；专辑 / The band released a new album last month.
alcohol /ˈælkəhɔːl/ n. 酒精；酒 / Excessive consumption of alcohol is harmful to health.
alert /əˈlɜːrt/ adj./v./n. 警觉的；提醒 / The government issued an alert about the approaching typhoon.
alien /ˈeɪliən/ n./adj. 外星人；外国的 / The concept of alien life fascinates many scientists.
